[2025-04-29 19:34:22] PROPOSAL by USA:
Title: Global Carbon Tax Framework: A Balanced Path to Climate Innovation
Action Item 1: Phased and Differentiated Implementation  
A globally coordinated carbon tax shall be introduced in stages, guided by each nation’s economic capacity and historical emissions. Developed nations will adopt higher initial rates, reflecting their greater ability to mitigate and their historic responsibility. Developing economies will phase in the tax more gradually, ensuring they can continue to foster growth and alleviate poverty. Annual reviews will ensure fairness and allow adjustments based on new technology or evolving economic circumstances.

Action Item 2: Technology and Innovation Incentives  
A share of carbon tax revenues will be allocated for research, development, and deployment of breakthrough clean technologies. This aims to accelerate innovation, reduce compliance costs over time, and provide targeted support for industry transitions. Dedicated funding will bolster technology transfer to developing nations, helping them leapfrog to clean energy solutions.

Action Item 3: Revenue Recycling for Equitable Transitions  
To build political viability, revenues will also be recycled domestically to address economic impacts, protect vulnerable populations, and enhance workforce retraining. Internationally, a portion of the revenues will go into a global Climate Solidarity Fund for adaptation and green infrastructure in lower-income nations, ensuring equitable development and boosting resilience against climate impacts.

This proposal seeks global consensus on a fair, ambitious policy to reduce emissions, drive innovation, and respect diverse national circumstances.

